  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Reader Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the user\'s request for \"reader functionality.\" I\'ve started by examining what this means in the context of the application. The app currently tracks manga, so the reader functionality would need to incorporate the source, and a way to read and track progress. My focus is on the scanlation site integration aspect.\n\n\n**Designing Reader Architecture**\n\nI\'m now diving into the core design of the built-in reader. My focus is on the \"Chapters & Reader\" component. I\'m exploring how it should look and function. I am considering its use in the `MangaDetailModal` and Library cards. A key element is the intuitive chapter list view. I\'m thinking about the user flow. I\'m focused on the \"Chapters & Reader\" entry point.\n\n\n**Developing Reader Options**\n\nI\'m now outlining the built-in reader\'s modes and features. I\'m focusing on user control. I envision vertical scrolling for manhwa/manhua, and single/double-page modes for manga. I\'ll include zoom, background color, fullscreen, and page gap adjustments. A chapter selector is planned for easy navigation, and automatic chapter marking as read.\n\n\n**Implementing Read-Progress Tracking**\n\nI\'m now implementing the read-progress functionality. I want to save time and make this work seamlessly. The goal is automated marking when 80% is reached or the end is hit. A floating bar with \"Mark Read & Next Chapter\" will improve the user experience. I am also making sure that reading position is saved.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Webtoon Rendering**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring consistent webtoon rendering. My immediate goal is a fallback mechanism using dynamic panel generation to handle potential 404 image errors. I\'m exploring a server route (`/api/reader/fetch-pages`) that takes key parameters to retrieve chapter details and image lists. This will allow the application to reliably load all chapters, even those with problematic image sources.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 733608249
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
