    thinking: "**Designing Reader API Endpoints**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on the `GET /api/reader/chapters/:mangaId` endpoint in `server.ts`. The plan is to return a chapter list for a given manga ID. The approach is to search the `mangaDatabase` and generate the chapters from 1 up to `manga.latestChapter`.\n\n\n**Refining Chapter Data Structure**\n\nI\'ve been focusing on the structure of the chapter data, considering how to handle sorting based on the `order` query parameter. Each chapter now includes the `id`, `chapterNumber`, `title`, `releaseDate`, `scanGroup`, `pageCount`, and `isRead` fields, all structured as requested.\n\n\n**Visualizing Interactive Panels**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to visualize webtoon panels. Each page will be styled with panel borders, sound effects, speech bubbles, poses, and episode progress. This creates an immersive experience that works offline and online. I\'m also planning a new `GET /api/reader/panel-image` to return dynamic SVG images, tailored to the manhwa/manhua genre, like level-up auras, Qi energy, or magic circles! I\'m also adding a POST endpoint to mark chapters as read.\n\n\n"
